# 09. Linux Input and Output Redirection

## 1. Introduction

Redirection allows Linux users to control where command input and output are sent.

It is commonly used in Linux administration and shell scripting.

## 2. Standard Input, Output and Error

Linux uses three standard streams:

| Stream | File Descriptor | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| stdin | 0 | Standard Input |
| stdout | 1 | Standard Output |
| stderr | 2 | Standard Error |

